# Normalize line endings: LF in the repo, checked out as-is.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.svg text eol=lf

# Search Console's verification file is a token, not prose, and `text=auto`
# above gives git permission to rewrite it. There is nothing to rewrite today —
# it is one line with no trailing newline — which is exactly why this is worth
# pinning rather than leaving to luck: the first editor that adds a newline, or
# a checkout that decides on CRLF, changes the bytes Google compares against the
# file it issued, and the property silently un-verifies. `-text` means "never
# convert line endings in this file"; the diff stays readable.
public/google7c8f404330a3c9e6.html -text
